.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-record-probe 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-record\-probe \- Run a probe command and record the family\*(Aqs reading of its exit status and output
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten record probe\fR [\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIfamily\fR> <\fIcommand\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a probe command and record the family\*(Aqs reading of its exit status and output
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<input>\fR
A `<key>=<value>` input this family needs beyond stdin (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIfamily\fR>
The record family, which selects the reading and is the key a module reads it under
.TP
<\fIcommand\fR>
The probe command, after `\-\-`: its exit status is the `status` input and its output the document
